<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Poland reaffirms support for Ukraine after drone strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ddcb7eb0b7c0539b55a7141da2a5149fb4913183e29e53b02fc6078ebbcdedb</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144--da0463d9d7dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Russia's recent drone attacks on targets close to the Ukraine-Poland border, Warsaw has doubled down on its support for Kyiv and pledged a "nonprovocative but serious response" to Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo ex-president Thaci sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e27127af6d6b029f346eed4454502ae8c61c14ccd9b892a4008a156efbc555fb</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344--737389b3e2ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Hague tribunal ruled that Hashim Thaci, a former leader of the Kosovo Liberation Army (KLA), is responsible for war crimes carried out during the war of independence with Serbia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's rights groups, EU call out LGBTQ+ crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f14ff007d2127ef5815098f65892b60cccc2dfea78902c1cf5f690156f060eb3</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021--701b89ffacea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several raids and arrests of LGBTQ+ persons in Turkey have triggered sharp criticism from numerous Turkish organizations — and also from Brussels.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why do authoritarian regimes target the LGBTQ+ community?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3d5e3e363106df26310cecc91723ab30922182ef18e17b0a27def4575689d2d</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831--8b4048f7a695.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A recent crackdown on the LGBTQ+ community in Turkey is symptomatic of a wider rights regression, according to experts. It's worse under authoritarian regimes, but why is it such a popular policy for these states?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Netherlands: Suspected sabotage disrupts train services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:598eb47ab6f8e96fde9edbeb636a43f4b7a5c861e7f1ce6a2dd2fbd0aa184239</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600--a0c80c1ea5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major outage has hit parts of the Dutch railway system after objects were found placed across lines, authorities say. The company responsible for rail infrastructure says it suspects deliberate wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Europe launches two climate observation satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:290ec0976973816f341b5d8a55279a24e00327ef57d5c207496fef25a2b57ccb</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705--7858649e62ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Space Agency has put two satellites into orbit to take a closer look at the impact of climate change. One of them will focus particularly on plant life.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks Arctic strategy amid growing power rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d21ad1b84f14ccde40662dc6c48237336a2ddc35d43e3055ff635c976351dd74</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739--8da58b1eb0cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's aggression, Trump's threats against Greenland and the race for critical raw materials are pushing the Arctic to the top of Europe's agenda.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia set for new round of US-mediated talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:741340a4905e3aa5e12718b72d3d055a6d18c77edec71e26c1f1d5648099c6d2</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T18:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147--0cf6c10eaa61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New trilateral talks between Ukraine, Russia and the US could begin in October, according to Kyiv and Moscow. Few expect a breakthrough, but Ukraine is seeking a partial de-escalation to help it get through the winter.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump seeks halt to energy attacks by both Russia, Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5eeaa4cfac65cf2f1373d58e3cce61c76773fbba43e0fc2443d5bd0f5dc77966</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774--121a884cf5a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump, under fire for record US diesel prices, claims Russia and Ukraine have agreed to stop striking energy targets. Russia said nothing; Ukraine said "we expect specifics from our partners" on any such move.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders urge unity after Russian strike on train</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae5a063e9d0e3e980c2504ed78535d29f5b732948870726b1fc5861dc2ad88a8</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807--826cde282d81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's drone attack on a train near the Ukraine-Poland border has triggered EU calls to up support for Kyiv. Allies of Ukraine should show they "are not scared," said the bloc's top diplomat, Kaja Kallas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russians on the Goethe-Institut: 'Hostage to politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3c6f530add9c4d256a3ff3f84d8dac74d056e4f5f4a195c79b60e79a19947dd</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936--8619b68c7998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia has affected their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A Romani artist in Hungary reclaims his identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96745361842d955cd5f27a441ab731feef905804c6c7369f2174d157136086cb</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266--3fed9cef9147.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Norbert Olah is an artist. He's also Romani. For a long time, he avoided making his ethnic background a theme of his art for fear of being pigeonholed. Then it became his focus.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's drone war comes to Moldova and Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f707a4429a7fdd7fdb2d8000db62fe62dd0bf4e3cf6c305fbc517bde9461f99</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591--15076a5f335b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Incursions by Russian drones into Moldovan and Romanian airspace are increasingly common. This week the Ukrainian president's plane was stopped from taking off from Chisinau. Observers suspect the attacks are deliberate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>DW exclusive: Zelenskyy offers to meet Putin at G20 in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d560d09955c031e60773c50d937d2f5ef6aee230b897266cd2c3b27a93068e25</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703--3aacfd955f7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an interview with DW, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said his country was in a strong position to negotiate and offered to meet Vladimir Putin in Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e8f7fff59c24fec2c7c181e3d76a2fc4e2499e8f94dfa7c925c830facd5695f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Magyar vs. Moscow: Hungary toughens stance toward Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:771476db4ea45a1e8ef3eeaa0ad1834d149cbbf6a1d4af2fe9d30642c54523d4</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-toughens-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424--a42f60a005da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-toughens-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Peter Magyar has abruptly ended the era of his predecessor's warm relations with Russia: Hungary has expelled 10 Russian diplomats. The Kremlin is considering halting gas supplies in response.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Are electric cars really bad for the environment?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cc20c05363a76c1c78c4cf95630604a58d8d477d05b3d86eba56b6d7415d513</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-electric-cars-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336--69d71b67dca0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-electric-cars-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some German politicians are calling for a delay to the EU plan to phase out gas-powered vehicles, saying cars must be judged on the entire carbon footprint. But the full picture still says EVs are more climate friendly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34e5679f071c6fcb4852b2cd9814d7fa529f160df8c7d61f3493d8be768913ce</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T05:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Putin rejects mobilization rumors, many Russians unconvinced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:756479a26b6c73a733e641a3ac184f304ecd1b06e76bf3aae0e5a1ab584a3c40</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386--b343555e2833.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia’s President Vladimir Putin has dismissed rumors about military mobilization. But many Russians, including many DW users, say they are preparing for the possibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German economy frets about Saxony-Anhalt election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a37f24238f57f69a8eefa6cb4f340094cd4040fabccc2beb83496bfef65b6515</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871--94d137604c23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD won the election in the eastern German state by a wide margin. While politicians and election analysts are still debating the reasons for the far-right party's popularity, economists are sounding the alarm.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
